{"page":152,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.20386,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"138 Chapter 3: Derivatives"},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.10752,"w":0.39349,"h":0.03283,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Derivative Constant Multiple Rule If u is a differentiable function of x, and c is a constant, then"},{"x":0.56597,"y":0.15014,"w":0.09792,"h":0.02729,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (cu) = c du"},{"x":0.64802,"y":0.15736,"w":0.02167,"h":0.02006,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.22874,"w":0.27104,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"In particular, if n is any real number, then"},{"x":0.14412,"y":0.24572,"w":0.0415,"h":0.01216,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"y = 3x2"},{"x":0.55635,"y":0.25134,"w":0.12296,"h":0.02729,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (cxn) = cnxn-1."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.28813,"w":0.03818,"h":0.01311,"fs":0.01311,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Proof"},{"x":0.19198,"y":0.30737,"w":0.07585,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Slope = 3(2x)"},{"x":0.50807,"y":0.30904,"w":0.12389,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"cu(x + h) - cu(x)"},{"x":0.42401,"y":0.31183,"w":0.08043,"h":0.02728,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d dxcu = lim"},{"x":0.66359,"y":0.31456,"w":0.11124,"h":0.02302,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Derivative definition with ƒ(x) = cu(x)"},{"x":0.225,"y":0.31879,"w":0.05997,"h":0.02231,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"= 6x = 6(1) = 6"},{"x":0.48132,"y":0.32879,"w":0.02453,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0"},{"x":0.09758,"y":0.33051,"w":0.12089,"h":0.01238,"fs":0.01023,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"3 (1, 3) Slope"},{"x":0.51529,"y":0.34651,"w":0.10943,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"u(x + h) - u(x)"},{"x":0.46434,"y":0.35584,"w":0.04734,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= clim"},{"x":0.56592,"y":0.35843,"w":0.27327,"h":0.01815,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"h Constant Multiple Limit Property"},{"x":0.22091,"y":0.35979,"w":0.03495,"h":0.01214,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"y = x2"},{"x":0.48855,"y":0.36626,"w":0.02453,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0"},{"x":0.46434,"y":0.38422,"w":0.04273,"h":0.01999,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= cdu"},{"x":0.49114,"y":0.39333,"w":0.26771,"h":0.01816,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dx u is differentiable."},{"x":0.19413,"y":0.42368,"w":0.06059,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Slope = 2x"},{"x":0.22734,"y":0.43519,"w":0.05997,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 2(1) = 2"},{"x":0.1914,"y":0.43671,"w":0.02981,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Slope"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.43705,"w":0.17881,"h":0.02984,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 2 (a) The derivative formula"},{"x":0.09758,"y":0.43859,"w":0.10843,"h":0.01602,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"1 (1, 1)"},{"x":0.5426,"y":0.4749,"w":0.1504,"h":0.02907,"fs":0.01918,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (3x2) = 3 # 2x = 6x"},{"x":0.09758,"y":0.49906,"w":0.08216,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"0 1"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.51317,"w":0.593,"h":0.01421,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"says that if we rescale the graph of y = x2 by multiplying each y-coordinate by 3,"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.52473,"w":0.23003,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01151,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 3.10 The graphs of y = x2"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.52994,"w":0.58888,"h":0.05116,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"then we multiply the slope at each point by 3 (Figure 3.10). (b) Negative of a function The derivative of the negative of a differentiable function u is the negative of the func-"},{"x":0.04848,"y":0.54008,"w":0.2292,"h":0.02813,"fs":0.01151,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"and y = 3x2. Tripling the y-coordinate triples the slope (Example 2)."},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.58297,"w":0.42331,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"tion’s derivative. The Constant Multiple Rule with c = -1 gives"},{"x":0.54385,"y":0.60446,"w":0.13551,"h":0.02907,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx (-1 # u) = -1 # d"},{"x":0.46954,"y":0.60624,"w":0.08611,"h":0.02729,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (-u) = d"},{"x":0.66757,"y":0.60624,"w":0.09275,"h":0.02729,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx (u) = - du"},{"x":0.74445,"y":0.61345,"w":0.02167,"h":0.02006,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.64414,"w":0.5929,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"The next rule says that the derivative of the sum of two differentiable functions is the sum of their derivatives."},{"x":0.0583,"y":0.66196,"w":0.24908,"h":0.11188,"fs":0.01151,"n":8,"k":1,"t":"Denoting Functions by u and Y The functions we are working with when we need a differentiation formula are likely to be denoted by letters like ƒ and g. We do not want to use these same letters when stating general differentiation rules, so instead we use letters like u and y that are not likely to be already in use."},{"x":0.35358,"y":0.73124,"w":0.53251,"h":0.04818,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Derivative Sum Rule If u and y are differentiable functions of x, then their sum u + y is differentiable at every point where u and y are both differentiable. At such points,"},{"x":0.63459,"y":0.78854,"w":0.05722,"h":0.02794,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx + dy"},{"x":0.53803,"y":0.78921,"w":0.11244,"h":0.02729,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (u + y) = du"},{"x":0.6757,"y":0.79642,"w":0.02193,"h":0.02006,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.86596,"w":0.59302,"h":0.03329,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"For example, if y = x4 + 12x, then y is the sum of u(x) = x4 and y(x) = 12x. We then have"},{"x":0.48956,"y":0.9066,"w":0.05171,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dy dx = d"},{"x":0.52947,"y":0.90905,"w":0.08395,"h":0.0276,"fs":0.01401,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx (x4) + d"},{"x":0.60162,"y":0.91111,"w":0.14448,"h":0.02524,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx (12x) = 4x3 + 12."}]}